            "label": "Name at the door",
            "sections": [
              {
                "heading": "Name at the door",
                "accent": "#2FBFA8",
                "text": [
                  "Flow 1 — hub-local face recognition on a motion event. The face gallery is enrolled on the LAN: the owner names a face crop in the app, Facewright embeds it on the NPU and back-tags past events; only a gallery version counter ever reaches Rollbook.",
                  "Foundry — firmware image staging; the hub pulls images and re-serves cameras."
                ],
                "bullets": [
                  "**Lookout B4's LP wake controller** trips on PIR and raises the video SoC's power rail.",
                  "The camera starts encoding and pushes the stream to **Fleetd** over LAN Wi-Fi, with its on-camera detector's person boxes muxed in as a metadata track.",
                  "**Fleetd** hands boxed frames to **Facewright**.",
                  "**Facewright** crops the face and runs the embedding on the Facet NPU (`34 ms`/frame).",
                  "**Facewright** matches against the gallery — \"Dana\", score `0.91` — and passes the identity to **Vaultd**.",
                  "**Vaultd** writes the clip with the identity tag and indexes the event.",
                  "The hub notifies **Beacon** over the control channel with text-only metadata: event id, camera name, \"Dana\". No pixels leave the LAN.",
                  "**Beacon** hands the notice to **Crier**, which pushes \"Dana at the driveway\" to the owner's phone; a LAN app fetches the thumbnail from the hub directly, an off-LAN app opens Flow 4."
                ],
                "contract": {
                  "title": "On the wire: control-channel event notice (hub → Beacon)",
                  "fields": [
                    {
                      "k": "hub_id",
                      "v": "K2-0F3A",
                      "g": "claiming hub"
                    },
                    {
                      "k": "event_id",
