                "accent": "violet",
                "text": [
                  "Flow 2 — cross-camera tracking and the one-clip incident."
                ],
                "bullets": [
                  "The driveway camera's event reaches **Stitcher**, which opens a track with a body re-ID embedding (works without a face).",
                  "**Stitcher** consults the adjacency graph and asks **Fleetd** to pre-wake the yard and porch cameras.",
                  "**Fleetd** sends wake commands so the battery cameras skip their own PIR wait.",
                  "The subject exits the driveway frame edge; **Stitcher** closes segment 1 and predicts the yard as next.",
                  "The yard camera streams; **Stitcher** matches the re-ID embedding at `0.87` and appends segment 2 to the same track.",
                  "The porch camera picks the subject up the same way; the track closes after `20 s` with no matches anywhere.",
                  "**Stitcher** pulls the three segments from **Vaultd**, trims dead air, and concatenates one incident clip with per-camera chapter marks.",
                  "**Vaultd** stores the assembled clip as a single event referencing its source segments.",
                  "**Crier** pushes \"One visitor crossed 3 cameras — 48 s clip ready.\""
                ],
