          {
            "label": "Seen from afar, read by no one",
            "sections": [
              {
                "heading": "Seen from afar, read by no one",
                "accent": "green",
                "text": [
                  "Flow 4 — remote viewing brokered through the relay."
                ],
                "bullets": [
                  "The off-LAN app asks **Beacon** for a session to hub `K2-0F3A`, presenting its auth token.",
                  "**Beacon** checks ownership with **Rollbook** and issues a session ticket plus a relay candidate list.",
                  "**Beacon** forwards the offer down the hub's persistent control channel to **Porter**.",
                  "**Porter** and the app exchange connectivity candidates through **Beacon** — signaling only.",
                  "A direct P2P path fails (symmetric NAT), so both sides attach to the same **Passage** relay node.",
                  "**Porter** derives the media key from the pairing secret shared at claim time — a secret the cloud never held.",
                  "**Passage** forwards encrypted frames both ways; it can count bytes but cannot decrypt one.",
                  "The app decrypts and renders the live view with a \"relayed\" path badge.",
                  "On teardown **Passage** logs byte counts only; off the hub's disk, the video exists nowhere at rest."
                ],
                "contract": {
